Earlier checkpoint — inquiry and the first common pass, 31 October 2026 (@hephaestus-history-11: 0, is #chapter) { r_00DB59454E2E7C89A50597E11B
Historical evidence recorded before the skeleton migration. Counts, pending statuses, temporary handles and next-step instructions describe that checkpoint; consult the current development Record before acting.

The first inquiry block is installed. Seven new lessons cover questions/evidence types, variation and uncertainty, comparisons and rival explanations, reconstruction, communication/teaching/preservation, an integrated study and review. Five existing metrology/computation lessons supply quantity definitions, procedures, sampling, a checkable computational claim and reporting. The thirteen-Record sequence is `inquiry-core`, `inquiry-claims`, `met-measurand`, `met-principle`, `inquiry-variation`, `inquiry-comparisons`, `met-sampling-target`, `rc-claim`, `inquiry-reproduction`, `met-measurement-records`, `inquiry-communication`, `inquiry-foundation-study`, `inquiry-foundation-review`. Original shared identities, prose, imports and prior routes are preserved. Advanced source assignments have explicit first-reading boundaries.

Original examples distinguish observed range from a common offset, correction from exact error knowledge, paired agreement from accuracy, and a fitted explanation from evidence that separates alternatives. The three-point length/time sequence fits both an affine response and a drifting offset; a proposed new observation makes their predictions differ, without claiming either model is established or that the observation occurred. The finite-population study enumerates all 45 unordered two-item samples from eight 1 mm and two 3 mm pieces: 28 sample means are 1 mm, sixteen are 2 mm and one is 3 mm. Their average is the population mean, 1.4 mm, while the chance of missing both thick pieces under the stated uniform design is 28/45. Repeated readings of one object do not substitute for this selection mechanism. No physical or educational experiment is claimed.

Exact rational arithmetic passed 925 comparisons: stated means, differences, intervals and model predictions; the 45 pairs; sampling identities across 360 small populations; and 81 common-shift cases. The paired mean difference is 0.25 mm, unchanged by a common 0.4 mm shift to both methods. Independent calculations and the original input meanings are described in the study so a reader can reconstruct the work.

Existing sources were reused. Bell's NPL issue-2 guide was retrieved as a 43-page PDF temporarily outside the repository after browser passage retrieval failed; contents and selected sections 1–2, 5.1–5.3 and 6.1–6.2 were inspected. VIM3 entries 2.3 and 2.26 were checked on the official annotated site. NIST/SEMATECH sections 5.3.3, 5.3.3.1 and 5.3.3.2 supply selected design reading. Wilson and colleagues' publisher metadata, CC Attribution notice, introductory summary and data-management passages were inspected. The PMC Peng link returned a browser-check page, so its existing identity and assignment remain with an explicit no-fresh-body-inspection note. Larger reading assignments and learner exercises are not claimed as completed inspections. No source media is stored in the repository.

Installed checks passed: warnings-as-errors Cargo check for resources/publication/tests; complete Hephaestus parsing with 2,896 files and 2,934 Records; register parsing with 262 Records; exact 92-Record common selection/reachability; six direct area edges; 1,560 discovered documents from all 59 authored entrances; 2,894 unique explicit Hephaestus identities; 29,268 local references; and preservation of all sixteen original subject compositions and the existing stock program. All 134 pending subjects remain pending. The Nix cache reported a transient ignored busy message during Cargo evaluation; the check itself completed successfully. Whitespace checks passed.

The six first blocks contain 85 learning Records in total: 48 area-opening/new lessons and 37 reused lessons. The six area maps and Hephaestus root bring the selected common graph to 92 Records. This is an inventory of this authored pass, not a completion percentage for the sciences. Each of the six whole area cores remains unfinished; none of the 134 subject scopes is retired.

Temporary evidence: `/tmp/inquiry-foundation-draft.json`, `/tmp/inquiry-foundation-checks.json`, `/tmp/inquiry-foundation-stage.json`, `/tmp/inquiry-foundation-installed.json`, `/tmp/inquiry-foundation-audit.json`, and `/tmp/audit-inquiry-foundation.py --installed`. Drafting, staging and installation already ran; do not rerun them over later work. Earlier audit counts belong to their earlier checkpoints.

